  "about": "Synthetic bodies the live API has not sent but may. A number no float can hold makes the body malformed, and so does text with a lone surrogate or nesting deeper than 127 levels, the most serde_json reads. A byte order mark before the body is dropped. Every implementation must reach the same outcome: ok, rejected (with the given code) or malformed. Only the field that carries the answer is strict (valid, found, or the list itself); any other field of the wrong type is read as absent. A unit or suggestion without its code is no answer, so it is dropped. A case may also expect facts about what was decoded: count (units or suggestions) and unit (whether a reverse answer has one).",
